description: Git and pull request conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

# Git

- Keep commits focused and meaningful.
- Do not mix unrelated changes.
- Prefer [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/): `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `ci:`, `chore:`, …
- Common scopes: `repo`, `ci`, `deps`, `docs`, `build`, `test`.
- Avoid committing generated files unless required.
- Do not rewrite history unless explicitly requested.

# Pull requests

- One concern per PR when possible.
- Fill the PR template.
- Ensure `dotnet build` and `dotnet test` pass locally before pushing.
